The source[1] disagrees with you.

I was giving the benefit of the doubt for most items, especially worn
items.  Assuming that nethack is similar to medieval Europe, how many
cloth items were made from plant sources, rather than wool?  Not that
many.  But I included all cloaks (one error -- alchemy smocks are
leather, according to the source).

I looked at the sources to get my list, and specifically excluded any 
made from LEATHER or BONE (I did miss all the horns in my initial search
though).

The few objects that aren't specifically animal-based that I included 
are worm teeth/crysknives (should be obvious), and all things using oil 
(misclassified brass lanterns as using oil, they don't seem to).

The oil may be debateable -- what was the primary source of oil?  
Animal or vegetable?  I'm not sure, especially in a medieval period 
that nethack seems loosely based upon.

